    </note>
    <p>Now we’ll factor the greatest common factor from a trinomial. We start by finding the GCF of all three terms.</p>
    <example number="10.87">
      <problem>
        <p>Factor: $$3y^{2} + 6y + 9.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite each term as a product using the GCF.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the GCF.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check by multiplying.</cell>
