    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="10.174">
      <p>Factor: $$6x^{2} + 42x - 12.$$</p>
    </note>
    <p>In the next example, we factor a variable from a binomial.</p>
    <example number="10.88">
      <problem>
        <p>Factor: $$6x^{2} + 5x.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$6x^{2} + 5x$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Find the GCF of $$6x^{2}$$ and $$5x$$ and the math that goes with it.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite each term as a product.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the GCF.</cell>
              <cell>$$x(6x + 5)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check by multiplying.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>$$x(6x + 5)$$$$x \cdot 6x + x \cdot 5$$$$6x^{2} + 5x✓$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
